# The operator's fleet, in Island Hop.
# The operator is the Makana account on the login page's "Operator" demo button.
# Every ferry these tests add is named "HumanTest test ferry"; "Start with: no test ferries"
# removes any that a failed run left behind (see e2e/states/no-test-ferries.ts).

Test: Operator adds a ferry and removes it again

  Start with: no test ferries

  As operator:
    go to fleet page
    should see "Fleet"
    click "Add Ferry"
    "Add New Ferry" dialog should be open
    type "HumanTest test ferry" in "Ferry Name"
    type "40" in "Passenger Capacity"
    in "Add New Ferry" dialog, click "Add Ferry"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/ferries
    backend should reply 201 Created
    should see "Ferry vessel registered successfully"
    "Add New Ferry" dialog should be closed
    in "HumanTest test ferry" row, click "Remove Ferry"
    in "Remove Ferry" dialog, click "Yes, Remove Ferry"
    backend should receive DELETE /api/v1/ferries/:id
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Vessel permanently deleted"


# The page lets 1 seat through (min="1"); the server wants at least 5.
Test: A ferry with fewer than 5 seats is refused by the server

  Start with: no test ferries

  As operator:
    go to fleet page
    click "Add Ferry"
    type "HumanTest test ferry" in "Ferry Name"
    type "3" in "Passenger Capacity"
    in "Add New Ferry" dialog, click "Add Ferry"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/ferries
    backend should reply 400 Bad Request
    should see "Capacity must be at least 5 seats"
    "Add New Ferry" dialog should be open


# Only spaces get past the browser's own "required", so the page's own check is what stops it.
Test: The ferry form stops before sending when the name is only spaces

  As operator:
    go to fleet page
    click "Add Ferry"
    type "   " in "Ferry Name"
    in "Add New Ferry" dialog, click "Add Ferry"
    should see "Please provide a Ferry Name."
    backend should not receive any request
    "Add New Ferry" dialog should be open
